issues.description:
The hidden unset variables come only from a struct literal of the !Move type in the same function, and only direct reads and borrows use them. Three kinds of read are accepted:
- a closure that reads `f.cur` or borrows f;
- a nested literal `Outer { f: Frame { buf } }`, then `o.f.cur`;
- a value built by a callee, `fn mk() -> Frame { Frame { buf } }`, then `let f = mk(); print(f.cur)`.
The interpreter then reads the field with no value and prints `<moved>`.
